\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 2021\'96present
\f0\b0 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 There is no equivalent fixed EIB country annex. NDICI\'96Global Europe/EFSD+ provides broad geographical coverage, but actual availability depends on programming, investment windows and guarantee agreements; pre-accession countries fall under IPA III rather than the NDICI geographic programmes. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2021/947/2021-06-14/eng?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 EUR-Lex}}\cell \lastrow\row
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 There are also three different concepts of \'93eligible\'94:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Potentially eligible
\f0\b0  \'97 named in a potential-country annex but not yet activated.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Legally eligible
\f0\b0  \'97 included in the operative country annex.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Operationally eligible
\f0\b0  \'97 legally eligible, with the necessary EIB framework agreement and no suspension on new signatures.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 That distinction is empirically important: under the 2014 mandate, the Commission counted 
\f1\b 64 legally eligible countries but only 57 with EIB framework agreements
\f0\b0 , while Russia was additionally subject to a signing suspension. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://data.consilium.europa.eu/doc/document/ST-12314-2019-INIT/en/pdf?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 data.consilium.europa.eu}}\
